504
00:20:10.712 --> 00:20:11.847
Sí. toot. toot.

505
00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.748
(speaking Minionese. shouting)

506
00:20:13.782 --> 00:20:15.384
Stop! Stop.

507
00:20:15.418 --> 00:20:17.386
You've ruined everything.

508
00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.288
It was a perfect scene.

509
00:20:19.322 --> 00:20:22.258
All that work. All that money.
All that effort.

510
00:20:22.291 --> 00:20:23.859
Uh... (speaks Minionese) No?

511
00:20:23.892 --> 00:20:25.161
-Get out of here.
-(Minions gasp)

512
00:20:25.194 --> 00:20:26.862
You. you. you. you.
you. you. you. you.

513
00:20:26.895 --> 00:20:27.896
-And you.
-Me?

514
00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:29.365
Definitely you. Get out!

515
00:20:29.398 --> 00:20:32.301
-Out! Out. out. out. out. out!
-(Minions whimpering)

516
00:20:32.335 --> 00:20:34.203
-Out!
-(yelps. whimpers)

517
00:20:36.272 --> 00:20:38.207
<i>Verschwindet!</i>

518
00:20:38.241 --> 00:20:39.942
Let's go again.

519
00:20:39.976 --> 00:20:41.310
MAN:
Uh. hey. boss.

520
00:20:41.344 --> 00:20:43.146
We're out of film.

521
00:20:43.179 --> 00:20:44.846
(exhales)

522
00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:47.416
This is not going
to go down well.

523
00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.818
♪ ♪

524
00:20:56.725 --> 00:20:58.060
(Klaxon horn honks)

525
00:21:02.731 --> 00:21:04.733
(muttering quietly in German)

526
00:21:06.801 --> 00:21:08.971
FRANK:
You tell that no-talent bum

527
00:21:09.005 --> 00:21:11.207
if he messes up again.
he's fired!

528
00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.476
And then send him
a bottle of champagne

529
00:21:13.509 --> 00:21:15.444
because it's his birthday.
(chuckles)

530
00:21:15.478 --> 00:21:17.947
Oh! There he is.

531
00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.916
-Our favorite director.
-(chuckles nervously)

532
00:21:19.949 --> 00:21:21.150
Hello. Mr. Bright.

533
00:21:21.184 --> 00:21:22.919
-Mr. Bright.
-Yeah. yeah. yeah.

534
00:21:22.952 --> 00:21:24.453
-(yells) -All right.
let's see what you shot.

535
00:21:24.487 --> 00:21:25.454
(strained grunting)

536
00:21:25.488 --> 00:21:27.023
Roll the scene. now.

537
00:21:27.056 --> 00:21:29.158
We are so excited to see it.

538
00:21:29.192 --> 00:21:30.359
Come on. let's go.

539
00:21:30.393 --> 00:21:32.161
Just so you know. Mr. Bright.

540
00:21:32.195 --> 00:21:33.795
we had... (gulps)

541
00:21:33.828 --> 00:21:36.065
a small problem.

542
00:21:36.098 --> 00:21:36.933
A problem?

543
00:21:36.966 --> 00:21:39.402
Is just a puzzle
for friends to solve.

544
00:21:39.435 --> 00:21:41.404
Problems cost money. Elwood.

545
00:21:41.437 --> 00:21:42.972
If this scene is terrible.

546
00:21:43.005 --> 00:21:47.076
you will never work
in this town again.

547
00:21:47.109 --> 00:21:48.344
But we're sure you'll do great

548
00:21:48.377 --> 00:21:50.379
in any number of other towns.
(chuckles)

549
00:21:50.413 --> 00:21:51.846
(Max chuckles weakly)

550
00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.382
Roll the scene. please.
and thank you.

551
00:21:53.416 --> 00:21:55.717
-(film projector clicking)
-(piano playing jaunty tune)

552
00:22:00.855 --> 00:22:02.959
♪ ♪

553
00:22:09.532 --> 00:22:12.335
(dramatic piano music plays)

554
00:22:17.473 --> 00:22:19.774
(whimpers):
Ooh. here we go.

555
00:22:19.808 --> 00:22:22.011
♪ ♪

556
00:22:22.979 --> 00:22:24.480
What is going on?

557
00:22:24.513 --> 00:22:27.116
MAX: I know. That's what I was
trying to tell you at the...

558
00:22:27.149 --> 00:22:28.184
(whimpers)

559
00:22:28.217 --> 00:22:29.884
(Frank grunts)

560
00:22:29.919 --> 00:22:31.820
What are those things?

561
00:22:31.853 --> 00:22:33.556
Uh... they. uh...

562
00:22:33.589 --> 00:22:35.024
FRANK:
You changed the whole scene.

563
00:22:35.057 --> 00:22:36.926
-(dramatic chords)
-MAX: But I didn't.

564
00:22:36.959 --> 00:22:39.894
I... oh. boy. I didn't.

565
00:22:39.929 --> 00:22:41.530
It's genius!

566
00:22:41.564 --> 00:22:42.999
What?

567
00:22:43.032 --> 00:22:44.533
(jaunty music continues)

568
00:22:44.567 --> 00:22:46.269
The scene. it's great.

569
00:22:46.302 --> 00:22:48.137
It's better than great.
I love it!

570
00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.973
Those sickly children.
oh. they're fantastic.

571
00:22:51.007 --> 00:22:52.575
They have to be in
every shot of the movie.

572
00:22:52.608 --> 00:22:54.210
Uh... yeah.

573
00:22:54.243 --> 00:22:56.245
(laughs nervously)
Okay. Absolutely.

574
00:22:56.279 --> 00:22:59.348
I'm going to get
my very good friends--

575
00:22:59.382 --> 00:23:01.951
just those. uh. uh.
what's their names--

576
00:23:01.984 --> 00:23:04.253
and put them in the movie!

577
00:23:04.287 --> 00:23:05.921
(laughs nervously)

578
00:23:05.955 --> 00:23:08.157
(music ends)

579
00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:09.191
Sam?

580
00:23:09.225 --> 00:23:10.825
Elwood?

581
00:23:10.859 --> 00:23:12.561
Would you mind playing it?

582
00:23:12.595 --> 00:23:14.063
All right.

583
00:23:14.096 --> 00:23:16.831
(playing "As Time Goes By")

584
00:23:17.466 --> 00:23:20.036
Ah. that's the stuff. Frankie.

585
00:23:20.069 --> 00:23:23.139
Ah. yes. it is. Elwood.

586
00:23:23.172 --> 00:23:26.175
Schnell! Schnell! Get me my car!

587
00:23:26.208 --> 00:23:28.177
-(Klaxon horn blaring)
-Faster. faster!

588
00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:30.546
We need to find them.
Where are they?

589
00:23:30.579 --> 00:23:31.880
Get out of the way!

590
00:23:31.914 --> 00:23:33.582
Move it. move it!

591
00:23:33.616 --> 00:23:35.084
(horns honking)

592
00:23:38.054 --> 00:23:39.422
SUFFRAGETTES (chanting):
Give women the vote!

593
00:23:39.455 --> 00:23:40.956
Give women the vote!

594
00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:42.591
-Give women the vote!
-Take the next right.

595
00:23:42.625 --> 00:23:44.327
They could be on Sunset.

596
00:23:45.628 --> 00:23:47.463
-Ah.
-Ah.

597
00:23:47.496 --> 00:23:49.498
Oh. looka! (speaks Minionese)

598
00:23:49.532 --> 00:23:50.933
Ooh. ooh. ooh!

599
00:23:50.966 --> 00:23:52.601
-(grunts)
-(speaks Minionese)

600
00:23:52.635 --> 00:23:54.370
(grunting)

601
00:23:54.403 --> 00:23:56.005
(Henry laughing) Mmm!

602
00:23:56.038 --> 00:23:57.373
(gasps) Hey. hey!

603
00:23:57.406 --> 00:23:59.442
(chattering in Minionese)

604
00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:02.912
(hocks. spits)

605
00:24:02.945 --> 00:24:04.180
Oh.

606
00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:05.981
(laughing)

607
00:24:06.015 --> 00:24:07.483
(speaking Minionese)

608
00:24:07.516 --> 00:24:08.584
Eh. looka.

609
00:24:08.617 --> 00:24:10.486
(hocks. spits)

610
00:24:10.519 --> 00:24:12.555
(laughter)

611
00:24:12.588 --> 00:24:14.657
(speaks Minionese. hocks. spits)

612
00:24:14.690 --> 00:24:16.625
-(laughter)
-VENDOR: Hey!

613
00:24:16.659 --> 00:24:18.527
-MEN: Huh?
-Don't let 'em get away!

614
00:24:18.561 --> 00:24:19.962
(angry shouting)

615
00:24:19.995 --> 00:24:21.530
-(police whistle blowing)
-Huh?

616
00:24:21.564 --> 00:24:23.366
(whimpering. screaming)

617
00:24:23.399 --> 00:24:24.633
-(shouting in Minionese)
-(whimpering)

618
00:24:24.667 --> 00:24:26.102
DICK:
Huh? (stammering)

619
00:24:26.135 --> 00:24:27.536
-(screams)
-(whimpering)

620
00:24:27.570 --> 00:24:29.038
(angry shouting)

621
00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:33.142
(frantic chattering)

622
00:24:34.443 --> 00:24:36.245
-(bicycle bell ringing)
-BICYCLIST: Whoa!

623
00:24:36.278 --> 00:24:38.280
-(tires screeching)
-(frantic chattering)

624
00:24:38.314 --> 00:24:39.415
(screams)

625
00:24:40.316 --> 00:24:41.283
(cries out)

626
00:24:41.317 --> 00:24:42.218
(neighing)

627
00:24:42.251 --> 00:24:44.620
-(Klaxon horn honks)
-(gasps)

628
00:24:44.653 --> 00:24:46.389
(Klaxon horn honks)

629
00:24:46.422 --> 00:24:47.456
(laughs):
My boys!

630
00:24:47.490 --> 00:24:50.226
I've been looking all over
for you. Get in. get in.

631
00:24:50.259 --> 00:24:51.961
-MAN: There they are!
-Uh...

632
00:24:51.994 --> 00:24:53.429
-(Dick yelps)
-Get those little guys!

633
00:24:53.462 --> 00:24:54.597
(shouts in Minionese)

634
00:24:54.630 --> 00:24:56.632
-Quick. quick.
-(grunting)

635
00:24:56.665 --> 00:24:58.033
DICK:
Go. go. go!

636
00:24:58.067 --> 00:24:59.935
(tires squealing)

637
00:24:59.969 --> 00:25:02.471
MAN:
Don't let them get away!

638
00:25:02.505 --> 00:25:04.273
MINIONS:
Banana!

639
00:25:04.306 --> 00:25:06.509
(excited chattering
in Minionese)

640
00:25:06.542 --> 00:25:09.578
(muffled chatter)

641
00:25:09.612 --> 00:25:11.380
(muffled laughing)

642
00:25:11.414 --> 00:25:12.982
(speaking Minionese)

643
00:25:13.015 --> 00:25:15.151
Wunderbar. Wunderbar.

644
00:25:15.184 --> 00:25:16.719
Uh. first things first.

645
00:25:16.752 --> 00:25:18.154
Who are you?

646
00:25:18.187 --> 00:25:19.622
-(speaks Minionese) ...Henry.
-Y James.

647
00:25:19.655 --> 00:25:21.290
(speaks Minionese) ...Dick.

648
00:25:23.192 --> 00:25:24.493
-(speaks Minionese) ...Ed.
-Uh...

649
00:25:24.527 --> 00:25:26.128
-Soy Peter!
-(speaks Minionese) ...Ken.

650
00:25:26.162 --> 00:25:29.465
(Minions shouting out names)

651
00:25:29.498 --> 00:25:31.033
(stammering)

652
00:25:31.066 --> 00:25:33.269
Is-is there a name
I can just call all of you?

653
00:25:33.302 --> 00:25:34.437
Bah...

654
00:25:34.470 --> 00:25:35.604
Minions.

655
00:25:35.638 --> 00:25:38.474
Look. Minions. my name is Max.

656
00:25:38.507 --> 00:25:39.742
MINIONS:
Bello. Max!

657
00:25:39.775 --> 00:25:41.710
Yeah. hi.

658
00:25:41.744 --> 00:25:44.013
Okay. I'm so sorry
about earlier.

659
00:25:44.046 --> 00:25:46.749
So. I would like
to work with you.

660
00:25:46.782 --> 00:25:48.717
We should make movies.

661
00:25:48.751 --> 00:25:50.052
-Movies?
-Movies?

662
00:25:50.085 --> 00:25:51.320
-Movies?
-Huh?

663
00:25:51.353 --> 00:25:53.389
You don't know what movies are?

664
00:25:53.422 --> 00:25:54.590
Mm...

665
00:25:54.623 --> 00:25:59.395
Movies are stories that
play out right in front of you.

666
00:25:59.428 --> 00:26:04.033
and people love them and people
love the people who make them.

667
00:26:04.066 --> 00:26:06.001
(speaks Minionese) ...storya.

668
00:26:06.035 --> 00:26:08.604
James... (speaks Minionese)
La storya.

669
00:26:08.637 --> 00:26:10.239
Le movies? ¿Para mí?

670
00:26:10.272 --> 00:26:12.374
-Sí. James. Sí!
-(James laughing)

671
00:26:12.408 --> 00:26:15.010
♪ ♪

672
00:26:15.044 --> 00:26:18.013
Welcome to
Bright Brothers Pictures.

673
00:26:18.047 --> 00:26:20.749
where we make
all kinds of movies.

674
00:26:20.783 --> 00:26:22.585
Oh. oh!

675
00:26:22.618 --> 00:26:24.186
(laughs)

676
00:26:24.820 --> 00:26:26.989
-Hello. Josh.
-JOSH: Hey. Sam.

677
00:26:29.258 --> 00:26:31.026
Perfect.

678
00:26:32.461 --> 00:26:34.430
(spluttering)

679
00:26:37.199 --> 00:26:39.068
All right. positions. everybody!

680
00:26:39.101 --> 00:26:41.070
-Find your mark...
-(busy chatter continues)

681
00:26:41.103 --> 00:26:43.272
♪ ♪

682
00:26:48.444 --> 00:26:50.312
(grunting)

683
00:26:52.414 --> 00:26:54.016
Whoo!

684
00:26:58.854 --> 00:27:00.289
-(cork pops)
-(cheering)

685
00:27:00.322 --> 00:27:02.558
It's a wrap.
Congratulations. everyone!

686
00:27:02.591 --> 00:27:04.093
(excited chatter)

687
00:27:04.126 --> 00:27:05.661
(stammers)

688
00:27:05.694 --> 00:27:07.630
Fantástico!

689
00:27:07.663 --> 00:27:08.797
It is fantástico.

690
00:27:08.831 --> 00:27:10.533
It's exciting. isn't it?

691
00:27:10.566 --> 00:27:13.202
Oh!
(speaking Minionese excitedly)

692
00:27:13.235 --> 00:27:15.504
Ah. James.
I love your enthusiasm.

693
00:27:15.538 --> 00:27:17.373
How about you gentlemen?

694
00:27:17.406 --> 00:27:19.441
-Do you want to make movies.
too? -(cheering)

695
00:27:19.475 --> 00:27:21.810
Eh. buh. buh. buh. buh.
No maka le movies.

696
00:27:21.844 --> 00:27:23.812
(speaking Minionese)
...Big Boss.

697
00:27:23.846 --> 00:27:25.281
-JAMES: Mm. -Uh...
-(shouting)

698
00:27:25.314 --> 00:27:27.216
-(laughter)
-Le movies!

699
00:27:27.249 --> 00:27:29.418
Excellent. Let's get to work.

700
00:27:29.451 --> 00:27:34.356
So. I need you to act
in a. mm. very simple scene.

701
00:27:34.390 --> 00:27:38.527
Here. You stay here.
and I shall return.

702
00:27:38.561 --> 00:27:39.795
Uh...

703
00:27:39.828 --> 00:27:41.363
-(lights thump)
-Oh.

704
00:27:41.397 --> 00:27:42.698
MAX:
Okay. listen up.

705
00:27:42.731 --> 00:27:44.233
So here's the scene.

706
00:27:44.266 --> 00:27:46.135
You see those large.
heavily armed men?

707
00:27:46.168 --> 00:27:48.837
They suspect you have killed
their leader.

708
00:27:48.871 --> 00:27:51.106
and they want you dead.

709
00:27:51.140 --> 00:27:52.174
(imitates slicing):
Gweek.

710
00:27:52.207 --> 00:27:53.475
Uh. gweek?

711
00:27:53.509 --> 00:27:55.244
-All right. I need you
-(whimpers)

712
00:27:55.277 --> 00:27:58.280
to really sell the drama.

713
00:27:58.314 --> 00:28:00.583
You do a good job.
and you're hired!

714
00:28:00.616 --> 00:28:03.652
You fail. it's back
to wandering the streets.

715
00:28:03.686 --> 00:28:05.287
scavenging for food.

716
00:28:05.321 --> 00:28:07.423
Have fun with it!

717
00:28:07.456 --> 00:28:08.557
Okay!

718
00:28:08.591 --> 00:28:10.726
Ready. action!

719
00:28:10.759 --> 00:28:11.894
-Attack!
-(angry shouting)

720
00:28:11.928 --> 00:28:13.195
(screaming)

721
00:28:13.228 --> 00:28:14.697
Uh. buddies? (screams)

722
00:28:14.730 --> 00:28:16.365
-(screams)
-(grunting)

723
00:28:16.398 --> 00:28:18.601
No. no. no. no. no! (screams)

724
00:28:18.634 --> 00:28:20.302
-(cries out)
-(yells)

725
00:28:20.336 --> 00:28:22.705
-(angry shouting)
-(whimpering) Henry!

726
00:28:22.738 --> 00:28:23.772
(whimpers)

727
00:28:23.806 --> 00:28:26.575
Henry. helpa! (whimpers)

728
00:28:26.609 --> 00:28:27.743
(growling)

729
00:28:27.776 --> 00:28:29.745
(shouting in Minionese)

730
00:28:29.778 --> 00:28:32.114
(grunting)

731
00:28:33.315 --> 00:28:35.217
Buddies! (speaks Minionese)

732
00:28:35.250 --> 00:28:37.386
-(chainsaw buzzing)
-(shouting)

733
00:28:40.222 --> 00:28:41.857
-(yells)
-Help!

734
00:28:41.890 --> 00:28:43.225
(grunts)

735
00:28:43.258 --> 00:28:45.260
-(laughing. munching)
-(screams)

736
00:28:46.963 --> 00:28:49.231
(screaming. grunting)

737
00:28:49.264 --> 00:28:51.166
-(yells)
-(pained grunt)

738
00:28:51.200 --> 00:28:52.167
(high-pitched scream)

739
00:28:52.201 --> 00:28:53.168
-Skoal!
-Skoal!

740
00:28:53.202 --> 00:28:54.737
-(grunts)
-(whimpers)

741
00:28:54.770 --> 00:28:56.805
-(whimpers)
-Hey.

742
00:28:56.839 --> 00:28:57.840
(screaming)

743
00:28:57.873 --> 00:28:59.274
Cut!

744
00:28:59.308 --> 00:29:00.910
-(stage bell ringing)
-(actors moaning)

745
00:29:00.944 --> 00:29:02.578
-Huh?
-(speaks Minionese)

746
00:29:02.611 --> 00:29:04.948
Okay. that was...

747
00:29:04.981 --> 00:29:07.650
(laughing):
perfect!

748
00:29:07.683 --> 00:29:09.752
(cheering)

749
00:29:11.286 --> 00:29:14.657
Minions. are you ready
to become stars?

750
00:29:14.690 --> 00:29:18.260
And I mean the biggest stars
the world has ever seen?

751
00:29:18.293 --> 00:29:20.429
(cheering excitedly)

752
00:29:20.462 --> 00:29:23.465
-(Max laughing)
-(cheering continues)

753
00:29:25.467 --> 00:29:26.802
(radio stations changing)

754
00:29:26.835 --> 00:29:28.704
-Honey. it's starting.
-(theme music playing)

755
00:29:28.737 --> 00:29:30.439
Oh. goodie.

756
00:29:30.472 --> 00:29:32.241
NARRATOR (over radio): On this
beautiful spring day of '27.

757
00:29:32.274 --> 00:29:34.410
<i>the world has never been</i>
<i>a better place.</i>

758
00:29:34.443 --> 00:29:36.612
<i>The economy is forever booming</i>

759
00:29:36.645 --> 00:29:39.415
<i>with no sign</i>
<i>of slowing down ever.</i>

760
00:29:39.448 --> 00:29:41.316
<i>People have never been so happy.</i>

761
00:29:41.350 --> 00:29:43.920
<i>and the future has never</i>
<i>looked so bright.</i>

762
00:29:43.953 --> 00:29:46.455
<i>Meanwhile. over in Hollywood.</i>

763
00:29:46.488 --> 00:29:48.490
<i>the new stars</i>
